  "query_preview": "..One more day of elevated fire weather conditions\nas upper level trof remains over the desert southwest. Highs\ntoday, the first day of July, will be similar to what occurred \nyesterday, the last day of June.\n\nThursday: Not as breezy with slightly warmer high temperatures.\n\nFriday: An upper high develops over NM with high temperatures a\nfew degrees warmer than Thursday. Mid-level moisture starts to\npush in from the south for scattered afternoon cumulus clouds.\n\n4th of July: On America's 250th birthday, moisture push\ncontinues with PWAT values between 0.70\" NE to 1\" west with the\nupper high over NM. Another afternoon of cumulus clouds. Highs \na few degrees above normal.\n\nSunday: Not much change in PWATs with slightly warmer highs.\n\nMonday and Tuesday: PWATs will be around normal to just above \nnormal early next week. This will be enough for a chance (10-40\npercent) for storms in the White Mountains and along the AZ/NM \nborder Monday with chances expanding west on Tuesday.",
